add('**VERIFIED mechanism / LIKELY projection weakness — team opportunity normalization mixes player histories from different teams and windows.** Gibbs’s recent 90.35% Detroit RB carry share is diluted to 55.67% when allocation includes unavailable Isiah Pacheco, whose latest three observed games are Kansas City Weeks 15–17 of 2025. After normalization, Pacheco’s 7.4206 allocated carries are removed without redistribution. Gibbs ends up with 10.7628 carries rather than his 17.0 prior-game average. Wilson’s targets similarly fall from an 8.0 recent average to 5.1600; unavailable NYJ histories consume 33.53% of normalized target volume. A 55% opportunity-anchor blend then reduces Gibbs’s mean by 4.4981 and Wilson’s by 3.7851. These are real upstream mechanisms, not an assertion that either corrected player must be selected.\n')
