add('### Gibbs: the model ranks him first, then spends elsewhere\n')
add('**VERIFIED:** Gibbs exceeds Brown by 2.0436 mean and the same 2.0436 P90, but costs $2,900 more. Brown has 12.1411 modeled carries versus Gibbs’s 10.7628; Gibbs has more targets (7.0523 versus 4.6867), making his opportunity anchor stronger. Warren offers 15.4781 mean / 28.6021 P90 at $6,700: $3,100 cheaper. Neither RB is “better” in absolute projection; they are more efficient ways to satisfy two mandatory RB slots while preserving strong WR/TE/stack combinations. Brown and Warren are both calibrated LEAD backs with the same +13.1240 P90 offset as Gibbs. Gibbs’s strong environment adds +1.2375 objective-context points, which helps him rather than suppressing him. His 35.2853% ownership does not penalize his objective because leverage is unavailable, and none of these diagnostic lineups approaches the 160% ownership ceiling.\n')
