add('## 6. Objective mathematics and scoring audit\n')
add('The exact original objective is:\n\n```text\nΣ [0.35 × (mean_i + context_i) / 27.678259770127184\n + 0.45 × (P90_i  + context_i) / 38.50809059260224\n + 0.05 × leverage_i / 1]\n + 0.15 × (active pair-rule adjustments + active format-rule adjustments).\n```\n')
add('The denominators are full eligible-pool maxima, computed before exposure blocking; they stay fixed across the sequential steps and forced-inclusion solves. Context is added to both mean and ceiling; the report splits it out as `context × (0.35/Mmean + 0.45/MP90)` to avoid attributing it to model truth. Context therefore carries an extra objective channel even though the nominal UI lists only four weights. Every reported component reconciles to the actual solver objective within 1e-7, and independent production-rule rescoring agrees.\n')
add('### Ceiling information and clipping\n')
add('**VERIFIED:** the Large-GPP path uses saved calibrated P90 directly, with no single-lineup upside-discovery clipping/saturation formula. Calibration adds empirical chronological residual quantiles to the conditional mean, with nonnegative/ordered quantile handling. There is no score cap that makes Gibbs and Garrett share an identical top score. Gibbs/Brown/Warren have exactly the same +13.12402633 P90 offset; Garrett/Metcalf/St. Brown/Michael Wilson share +12.87815501. Within each such bin, a one-point mean gain creates the same one-point P90 gain: the nominal ceiling term supplies no new within-bin upside ranking. Across bins it supplies meaningful, but coarse, distribution information.\n')
table(['Position','Players','Distinct P90−mean offsets','Largest repeated bin'],[[pos,sum(v.values()),len(v),max(v.values())] for pos,v in r['calibration_offsets'].items()])
add('The $3,400 TeSlaa gets +9.69288017 P90 above 8.24828245 mean. That cohort offset plus a fixed roster size can reward cheap role-bin members without a player-specific tail model. **LIKELY:** salary-efficient cohort ceilings encourage the repeated cheap/favored stacks. **NOT ESTABLISHED:** the residual quantiles are miscalibrated for these players, or an individually conditional tail model would improve out-of-time contest outcomes. The archived Week 3 prelock pool also shows repeated role/position offsets; only its frozen inputs were read, not its outcomes.\n')
add('### Correlation scale and favored games\n')
add('**VERIFIED:** pair and format terms are unnormalized policy points, whereas player mean/P90 terms are normalized individually then summed. “15% correlation” is a coefficient, not a promise that correlation constitutes 15% of the final score. Tight A has 0.109028571 correlation; broad A has 0.429767411 (8.66% of total). Broad A has three Detroit pass catchers, even though the first template requires only one. QB-pass-catcher pair rewards accumulate alongside a double-stack format reward and a competitive-game-stack reward. Per-rule signals are bounded; the original Large-GPP selection does not apply the separate single-lineup/captain saturation policy to erase these extra classic stack rewards.\n')
