add('### Why leverage is zero, and role-based correlations are unavailable\n')
add('`tag_players` calculates `optimal_lineup_probability − ownership` only when both exist; otherwise leverage is zero. **VERIFIED:** ownership exists but all 121 optimal-lineup probabilities are null, so all 121 leverage values and selected lineup contributions are zero. Ownership availability selects the 45/35/15/5 branch; actual leverage support does not activate any signal here, and the unused 5% is not redistributed. This is an availability/reporting mismatch, not clipping and not low ownership exactly offsetting high ownership. Ownership still affects hard caps/tags, which the controlled ablations show are not the cause here.\n')
add('**VERIFIED:** all 121 `optimizer_receiving_role_strength` and `optimizer_rushing_role_strength` values are zero. The source derives them from explicit forward role evidence (shares/expected counts/routes), which is missing for these eight, while lagged opportunity projections do exist. The adapted `Player` exposes the explicit zero, so correlation does not infer a receiving-back strength from Gibbs’s 7.0523 projected targets. QB + same-team WR/TE can earn its role reward; Goff + Gibbs cannot earn the receiving-back rule. **LIKELY:** this evidence gap favors pass-catcher constructions relative to legitimate receiving RB alternatives; the magnitude of an evidence-backed corrected signal is NOT ESTABLISHED. No synthetic strength or player-specific reward was added.\n')
